 "about": [
  "Hakutsuru Shuzo brews in Mikage, one of the five historic sake districts of Nada in Kobe. It traces its start to 1743, when a timber merchant named Jihei began brewing, and the Hakutsuru name was adopted in 1747. The family shares its ancestry with the Kano family behind Kiku-Masamune.",
  "In 1952 it built Japan's first reinforced concrete sake brewery. It also bred its own sake rice, Hakutsuru Nishiki, registered as a variety in 2007.",
  "Since 1982 a restored early brewery building has housed the company's sake museum."
